  "title": "Crypto Infrastructure Hub",
  "bluf": "The Hub now opens as a searchable visual atlas: every primary infographic has a direct front-page entrance, an embedded-view directory lands on the exact Fed, map, X-ray, legal, transition, liquidity, company or stack subview, and full-content search finds remembered terms inside entity records, explanations, relationships, process steps, legal questions, evidence boundaries, source labels and governed structured data rather than matching titles alone. The atlas is organized into four investigative workspaces—Systems & entities, Transactions, Rules & permissions, and Qualification & evidence—while preserving every governed owner and legacy room link. Transactions use X-ray as the layered control surface; Rules compares legal packages through a common authority, subject, clock and receipt frame; Qualification keeps functional fit, legal seat, exact route, operating receipt and scale/stress separate. The dedicated Fed GENIUS proposed-rule room still reads the paired 452-page package through a legal-entity map, seven institutional layers, twelve issuer and operating gates, nine clocks, all 277 questions and exact impacts across all twenty governed ecosystems. Transition Gates tests fourteen end-to-end requirements across thirty-four technology families, and no reviewed stack reaches complete R6 legacy retirement.",
